{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70fdfe609316eaf70b80ebd4b089aa2325b56af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TQ = TR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, what is the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1e8f13b12802e1d5e38ed3615bea901b7b835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PTRS$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/9844048c7ecfc656f5c3bb206c26551f4b45c170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49aa7d104cdfc1a20e51aa1a1706f259f5ebfbe1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); draw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4)--(0,4)--cycle); draw((0,4)--(6,2)); draw((5.8,1.1)--(6.2,1.1)); draw((5.8,.9)--(6.2,.9)); draw((5.8,3.1)--(6.2,3.1)); draw((5.8,2.9)--(6.2,2.9)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(0,4),NW); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(6,0),SE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;,(6,2),E); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,(6,4),NE); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"128\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, let us assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/febd82f6c40aa54bd8a8c0d17d8838b13dece237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1a84353a2870a9cc34f1b6e6d9f6b8e16a6bad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2364e26c9726aabaf12a17332d7594254461b984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT = TR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b489716975719fed982cccaf8dacb53e28b12b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 2QT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edf9e8024cda904caa0697239cf95a1dd9fb0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />.  Therefore, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005c541ad5c6447107888a658f3dacf93f812c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67b8642935b24d120f8224fb7971f0c75098009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> of length 2, so its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cfef41666a6839debbc1b2cb7ffc60a05657b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(6)(2) = \\frac{1}{2}(12) = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"162\" height=\"37\" />.\nSo the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1e8f13b12802e1d5e38ed3615bea901b7b835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PTRS$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />) minus the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005c541ad5c6447107888a658f3dacf93f812c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw a line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> across the rectangle parallel so that it cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805452ee372321839953fbd750cd9b23b973a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9091b433190b90db262d1c625217d6500599246b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SVTR$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> is a rectangle which has an area equal to half the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a10e97fa5b1ab7990347c849dc22b6d11cbb2e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VPQT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> is a rectangle of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a10e97fa5b1ab7990347c849dc22b6d11cbb2e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VPQT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> is cut in half by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdc03b4e24dbee7b5747d6a0aa2def18f5541d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, so triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9086b9ccef9729b4f286557b8caaf5119c9363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PVT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nTherefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1e8f13b12802e1d5e38ed3615bea901b7b835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PTRS$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the sum of the area of the rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9091b433190b90db262d1c625217d6500599246b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SVTR$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> and the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9086b9ccef9729b4f286557b8caaf5119c9363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PVT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8ea43fd0f5c0d66f1f150de3b8c86e22da1dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 6 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.  The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017100514\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 337/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2333/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 593/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8755/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.451      1 Template:CEMC_box\n100.00%    7.451      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13694:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017100514 and revision id 65651. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}